message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Differentiable Digital Twin: gradient-based structural inverse design with a WebGPU player"
abstract: >-
  An end-to-end demonstrator of differentiable physics for engineering design. A linear-elastic
  truss is assembled and solved in PyTorch and differentiated end-to-end, so a material
  distribution is optimised for minimum compliance by backpropagation through the solver. The
  optimised trajectory is replayed in a dependency-free WebGPU browser player. Includes a
  reproducible benchmark quantifying the asymptotic speedup of gradient-based over derivative-free
  (black-box) optimisation.
